Dear Adjudicating Officer:

I. INTRODUCTION

We respectfully submit this Form I-140 petition on behalf of Mr. Chen Xiaochun, requesting classification as an alien of extraordinary ability in the field of film and television production, screenwriting, and academic research pursuant to section 203(b)(1)(A) of the Immigration and Nationality Act and 8 CFR 204.5(h)(3). 

Mr. Chen is a distinguished professor, pioneering researcher, and accomplished practitioner who has made extraordinary contributions to China's film and television industry over more than two decades. He is recognized as the founder of China's first film and television production management academic program and has established groundbreaking evaluation systems that have transformed the industry. His scholarly works serve as authoritative textbooks throughout China, his creative works have achieved massive commercial success, and his expertise is regularly sought by major media organizations and government institutions.

This petition demonstrates that Mr. Chen meets multiple criteria under 8 CFR 204.5(h)(3) and that his planned continued work in the United States will substantially benefit the nation's film and television industry and academic institutions.

II. BACKGROUND AND QUALIFICATIONS

Mr. Chen holds a Bachelor of Arts degree in Chinese Language and Literature from Hunan Normal University (1983) and a Master of Arts degree in World Literature from Peking University (1989). His academic career spans over 25 years, during which he has held progressively senior positions at China's most prestigious media university - Communication University of China (formerly Beijing Broadcasting Institute).

Currently serving as Professor at the Art Research Institute of Communication University of China, Mr. Chen has:

• Established China's first film and television production management academic program
• Founded and directs the Film and Television Project Evaluation and Research Center
• Published 10+ academic books that serve as standard textbooks in Chinese universities
• Created and produced television series with over 680 million views
• Trained hundreds of successful producers, directors, and screenwriters
• Served as a key advisor to major Chinese media organizations and government institutions

III. EVIDENCE OF EXTRAORDINARY ABILITY

Mr. Chen's extraordinary ability is demonstrated through multiple regulatory criteria:

A. ORIGINAL CONTRIBUTIONS OF MAJOR SIGNIFICANCE (8 CFR 204.5(h)(3)(v))

Mr. Chen has made groundbreaking contributions that have fundamentally transformed China's film and television industry:

1. **Pioneer of Film and Television Production Management Education**: Mr. Chen created China's first film and television production management academic program at Communication University of China, establishing the theoretical foundation and practical curriculum for an entire new field of study. This program has become the model for similar programs throughout China. (Exhibit 1.5, 5.1)

2. **Founder of Film and Television Project Evaluation Systems**: Mr. Chen established the Film and Television Project Evaluation and Research Center and developed China's first systematic evaluation framework for television dramas. His methodology, detailed in his seminal work "The Script Doctor," has been adopted industry-wide and is taught in 8 advanced workshops attended by over 280 industry professionals from major platforms including iQiyi, Tencent, Youku, and provincial television stations. (Exhibit 3.1, 5.1, 5.2)

3. **Creator of Producer Training Programs**: In collaboration with the China Radio and Television Association, Mr. Chen developed and managed four intensive producer graduate training programs that trained many of China's most successful producers and directors, including those who later won Flying Sky Awards and Golden Eagle Awards. (Exhibit 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 2.4)

4. **Academic Innovation in Screenwriting Theory**: Mr. Chen's scholarly works have established new theoretical frameworks for screenwriting and production management that are now standard curriculum in Chinese universities. His book "TV Drama Theory and Creative Skills" was officially recognized as an excellent textbook by Beijing Higher Education authorities. (Exhibit 3.2, 3.3, 3.4)

B. AUTHORSHIP OF SCHOLARLY ARTICLES (8 CFR 204.5(h)(3)(vi))

Mr. Chen is the author of extensive scholarly publications that have established him as a leading authority in his field:

**Academic Books (10 publications):**
• "The Script Doctor – TV Drama Project Evaluation and Case Studies" (Exhibit 3.1)
• "Film and Television Production Management: from Project Planning to Marketing" (Exhibit 3.2)
• "TV Drama Theory and Creation Techniques" (Exhibit 3.3)
• "Principles of Screenwriting" (Exhibit 3.4)
• "The Theory and Practice of Screenwriting" (Exhibit 3.5)
• "Television Drama Production: from Project Planning to Marketing" (Exhibit 3.6)
• "A Perspective on the Chinese Film and Television Market" (Exhibit 3.7)
• "The Road to University: ways to enter art schools and how to take the exam" (Exhibit 3.9)
• "Art Exam Tips: A Practical Guide for Art Majors" (Exhibit 3.10)
• "TV Drama Creation--Theory, Techniques, and Case Studies" (Exhibit 3.12)

**Literary Works:**
• "Love at the End of the Century" (Exhibit 3.8)
• "Purgatory 1989" (Exhibit 3.11)
• "Fantasy Empires" (Exhibit 3.12)

These publications are widely distributed through major platforms including Amazon, JD.com, Douban, and other major Chinese book retailers, with extensive positive reviews and high circulation numbers documented in the exhibits.

C. PUBLISHED MATERIAL ABOUT THE PETITIONER (8 CFR 204.5(h)(3)(iii))

Major media outlets have published extensive coverage of Mr. Chen's work and achievements:

1. **NetEase/163.com Coverage**: Multiple articles highlighting Mr. Chen's role in developing TV drama evaluation systems and his leadership in the Film and Television Project Evaluation and Research Center (Exhibits 4.1, 4.2)

2. **Communication University of China Publications**: Official university publications documenting Mr. Chen's critical role as Executive Producer and Chief Screenwriter of "Shagen into the City," which exceeded 180 million views (Exhibit 4.3)

3. **SINA Coverage**: Articles discussing Mr. Chen's expertise in film and television project evaluation and his analysis of major productions (Exhibit 4.6)

4. **National Media Recognition**: Coverage in China.huanqiu.com and chinanews.com highlighting Mr. Chen's expertise and participation in high-level industry discussions (Exhibits 4.7, 4.8)

5. **Academic Recognition**: Publication in the authoritative "60 Years of Chinese Television Series: Volume on People" under the Teaching and Research chapter (Exhibit 5.3)

D. LEADING OR CRITICAL ROLE IN DISTINGUISHED ORGANIZATIONS (8 CFR 204.5(h)(3)(viii))

Mr. Chen has served in leadership positions in several distinguished organizations:

1. **Director, Film and Television Project Evaluation and Research Center**: Mr. Chen founded and directs this prestigious research center at Communication University of China, which serves as the primary institution for film and television project evaluation research in China (Exhibits 5.1, 6.1)

2. **Key Member, China Video Ranking Recommendation Committee**: Mr. Chen serves as a critical member of this national committee responsible for evaluating and recommending video content across China's major platforms (Exhibits 5.2, 6.2)

3. **Chief Executive Officer/Chairman**: Mr. Chen has been appointed as CEO or Chairman of three major film and television production companies:
   - Tianma Shenlong Film and Television Culture Communication Co., Ltd. (General Manager, 2012)
   - Jiuling Film and Television Culture Communication Co., Ltd. (General Manager, 2013)
   - Juxing Film and Television Culture Communication Co., Ltd. (Chairman, 2017-present)

E. RECEIPT OF LESSER NATIONALLY RECOGNIZED AWARDS (8 CFR 204.5(h)(3)(i))

Mr. Chen has received multiple prestigious awards and recognitions:

• **Academic Recognition**: Selected for inclusion in "60 Years of Chinese Television Series: Volume on People" by China Radio, Film, and Television Press (Exhibit 5.3)

• **Teaching Excellence**: Beijing Broadcasting Institute "Top 10 Teachers" Award (Exhibit 6.1)

• **Professional Achievement**: CCTV Outstanding Class Teacher Award (Exhibit 6.1)

• **Industry Recognition**: iQiyi Best Public Reputation Award for "Shagen into the City" (Exhibit 6.1)

• **Academic Excellence**: His book "TV Drama Theory and Creative Skills" was designated as an excellent textbook by Beijing Higher Education authorities (Exhibit 6.1)

• **Institutional Achievement**: Communication University of China Outstanding Achievement Award for "Shagen into the City" (Exhibit 6.1)

F. EVIDENCE OF JUDGING THE WORK OF OTHERS (8 CFR 204.5(h)(3)(iv))

Mr. Chen regularly serves as a judge and evaluator for major industry and academic institutions:

1. **China Video Ranking Committee**: Long-term service as judge for China's premier video content evaluation system (2017-2020) (Exhibit 5.2)

2. **Academic Bridge Evaluation Expert**: Appointed by China Society of Education Development Strategy as expert database member (2024)

3. **CCTV Anniversary Celebrations**: Regular invited judge for CCTV's 50th and 60th anniversary celebrations of Chinese television dramas, providing expert commentary on major productions including "Soldiers' Assault"

4. **Film and Television Project Evaluation**: Since 2006, Mr. Chen has evaluated numerous major film and television projects including "National Action," "Fox Hunt," "Sharp Knife," "Cherry," and "Shagen into the City"

IV. SUSTAINED NATIONAL AND INTERNATIONAL ACCLAIM

Mr. Chen's work has garnered sustained acclaim both nationally and internationally:

**National Recognition:**
• His academic programs and evaluation systems have been adopted throughout China's film and television industry
• His textbooks are standard curriculum in Chinese universities
• His television productions have achieved massive commercial success with hundreds of millions of views
• He is regularly invited as an expert commentator by national media outlets

**International Recognition:**
• His documentary film "Next Flowers" won two awards at the Warsaw International Film Festival (2023)
• His novels have been published internationally through Amazon and other platforms
• He serves as doctoral supervisor for international programs in Thailand
• His work has been translated and distributed in multiple countries

V. CONSULTATION LETTERS

This petition includes recommendation letters from distinguished experts in the field:

• **Director Mingzhi Zhang** (Exhibit 2.1): Provides expert assessment of Mr. Chen's contributions to the field
• **Professor Junqi Yan, Ph.D.** (Exhibit 2.2): Details Mr. Chen's academic achievements and influence
• **Professor Jinzhou Ren** (Exhibit 2.3): Confirms Mr. Chen's standing in the industry
• **Director Shan Bai** (Exhibit 2.4): Attests to Mr. Chen's practical contributions and leadership

VI. COMMERCIAL SUCCESS AND PRACTICAL IMPACT

Mr. Chen's work extends beyond academic achievement to substantial commercial success:

**Television Productions:**
• "Shagen into the City" - Over 680 million views, iQiyi Best Public Reputation Award
• "Tea Horse Ancient Road" - Broadcast on CCTV1
• "Sharp Knife" - Multi-platform broadcast
• "Cherry" - Four satellite TV broadcast

**Film Productions:**
• "Next Flowers" - Two Warsaw International Film Festival awards

**Business Leadership:**
• Successfully managed three film and television production companies
• Generated significant revenue and employment in the industry
• Developed innovative production and evaluation methodologies

VII. PLAN FOR CONTINUED WORK IN THE UNITED STATES

Mr. Chen's planned work in the United States will substantially benefit the nation through:

1. **Academic Collaboration**: Establishing partnerships between U.S. and Chinese film schools to develop international curricula and exchange programs

2. **Industry Innovation**: Bringing his proven evaluation and production management methodologies to American film and television companies

3. **Cultural Bridge Building**: Facilitating co-productions and cultural exchange between American and Chinese entertainment industries

4. **Educational Development**: Contributing to American film schools' curricula and training programs

VIII. CONCLUSION

Mr. Chen Xiaochun is an alien of extraordinary ability whose contributions to film and television production, screenwriting, and academic research have transformed an entire industry. His work has established new theoretical frameworks, created successful commercial productions, and trained hundreds of professionals who continue to shape China's entertainment landscape.

The extensive evidence submitted with this petition, including comprehensive documentation of his publications, media coverage, awards, leadership roles, and expert evaluations, clearly demonstrates that Mr. Chen meets multiple criteria under 8 CFR 204.5(h)(3) and possesses the extraordinary ability that qualifies him for the EB1A classification.

Mr. Chen's continued work in the United States will substantially benefit the nation's film and television industry, academic institutions, and cultural exchange programs. We respectfully request that USCIS approve this petition and grant Mr. Chen the EB1A classification he has clearly earned through his extraordinary achievements.

We thank you for your consideration of this petition and remain available to provide any additional information or clarification that may be required.

